chat - enter a chat room

usage: chat [room]

    Without a number it lists rooms then asks for one.
    After entering, the prompt is your own ID (e.g. "sysop> "). Lines you
    type are shown as-is as speech lines.

    The three venues (chat / talk / notes/mail/news) share the same keys.
    In speaking venues (chat / talk) you prefix with "/".
      /i  show the list (rooms)  * empty Enter also redraws
      /q  leave (. / q also work)
      /?  help (/help also works)

    /who shows occupants. /title changes the title.
    /! <id> <body> sends a private telegram without leaving the room
    (a bare ! inside a room is speech).
    /e toggles echoback (reflect your own line after sending; off by default).
